# What this plugin is, for the index in README.md and for whoever installs
# it alone. One key per line, a key repeated for each line of a message;
# ./install.sh at the repository's top installs it from the lines below.
name: xymonapi-rag
version: 0.1.0
side: server, client
summary: a search of Xymon's manual pages and history by meaning; the index task on the server, search and ask anywhere
requires: xymonapi >= 0.1.0 (its client beside it; the API beside it on the server, over the network elsewhere), python >= 3.9
manual: xymonapi-rag.1

# How ./install.sh installs it: see xymonapi's PLUGIN file.
needs: xymonapi
server-root: ext
server-roles: server
server-files: xymonrag.py xymonapi-rag.sh requirements.txt
server-manual: xymonapi-rag.1
server-modules: fastembed numpy
server-task: xymonapi-rag.tasks.DIST
server-removed: Removed xymonapi-rag. Kept: its index, $XYMONAPI_RAG_INDEX, and xymonapi.
tools-root: prefix
tools-roles: tools
tools-files: xymonrag.py xymonapi-rag.sh requirements.txt
tools-manual: xymonapi-rag.1
tools-modules: fastembed numpy
tools-venv-note: only to keep an index on this machine: search and ask through the server need none
tools-command: xymonapi-rag xymonapi-rag.sh
executable: xymonapi-rag.sh
tools-removed: Removed xymonapi-rag. Kept: xymonapi's client, and any index here, $XYMONAPI_RAG_INDEX.
